# failure-mode-guard matrix — loam's protection pillar as a living,
machine-checkable catalogue — apply ladder

Per `docs/plans/failure-mode-guard-matrix.md` and parent doctrine
`docs/design/loam-doctrine.md` §"The two sides of leg 2 —
translation in, protection around" (the protection pillar this
component operationalises).

Plan: `docs/plans/failure-mode-guard-matrix.md`.

Scope (per plan §2 + §6 + §7): NEW component
`framework/protection-matrix/`. loam's protection guards — today
implicit across nine release gates, a dozen hooks, ODD, file-based
memory, and the audit comparator — become an EXPLICIT, single-
source, living, machine-checkable catalogue: each known way an AI
betrays a user by default × loam's actual guard × whether that
guard is default-on × floor-vs-proportional × how we verify it
fires. A `loam guards` coverage-check verb derives the live guard
set from ground truth, reconciles it against the catalogue, and
NAMES the gaps (floor-class failure modes with no default-on
programmatic guard — the actionable output).

AC families:

  - AC.FMG-CAT.1 — the manifest at data/failure-mode-guard-matrix.yaml
    parses; every row carries every plan-§5 field with an enum-valid
    value.
  - AC.FMG-CAT.2 — every row whose guard_kind is not none/persona-
    discipline binds a guard_ref that resolves to a real path+symbol
    at check-time; an unresolved guard is reported (no invented
    coverage — the protection pillar must not itself hallucinate).
  - AC.FMG-CHECK.1 — `loam guards` is registered through the
    loam.cli.subcommands entry-point group (sibling to `loam audit`
    / `loam release`), runs against the live tree, and emits a
    floor-class coverage report.
  - AC.FMG-CHECK.2 — the check derives the guard set from GROUND
    TRUTH (settings hook registrations + the release ALL_GATES
    tuple) and reconciles against the manifest; a manifest claim of
    default_on:YES that ground truth contradicts is flagged as a
    divergence (mirrors the substrate-audit comparator).
  - AC.FMG-LIVE.1 — the catalogue refresh is registered as an item
    in loam's EXISTING recurring maintenance/pruning flow (doctrine
    §3 recurring schedule), NOT a net-new launchd/cron entry
    (Lens 1).
  - AC.FMG-GAP.1 — a run against the actual guard set emits, as a
    distinct section, the floor-class failure modes whose
    default_on != YES (the gaps); non-empty iff such modes exist.
  - AC.FMG-S.1 ★ (outcome-altitude) — the production `loam guards`
    entry-point, invoked with NO pre-arranged state against the
    REAL installed guard set, succeeds, asserts the floor invariant
    (every class:floor row checked for a default-on guard), and
    emits each uncovered floor row in the gap section. A STUB-class
    test that pre-seeds the manifest does NOT satisfy this AC
    (feedback_test_outcome_altitude_required).

Method-level choices are the builder's call per ODD §1.1; the plan
fixes the schema (§5), the row set (§5 table), and the entry-point
composition (loam.cli.subcommands), not the implementation.

The LOAD-BEARING finding (plan §10 F2): four-to-five floor-class
failure modes are today guarded ONLY by persona discipline
(FM.NARRATION-NOT-ACTION, FM.ENV-PERCEPTION-MVC,
FM.PROCESS-DRIFT-UNDER-PRESSURE, partially FM.BUILT-NE-LIVE /
FM.DESTRUCTIVE-PRUNE) — prose rules the doctrine itself says "decay
first under pressure," each born from a real recurring failure.
These ship as VISIBLE `default_on: NO-PROGRAMMATIC` gap rows, not
omissions; the gap report drives downstream structural-enforcement
cycles (feedback_structural_enforcement_on_recurrence). Building the
missing guards is OUT of scope (plan §7) — downstream, per-gap,
proportionality-prioritised.

Out of scope (plan §7): authoring new guards to close the gaps;
the release-gate HARD-block arm (check_floor_guards_present —
FORK F-4); auto-remediation; per-user proportional-tier tuning.

