# protection-matrix follow-on — track the catalogue + add the two
owed rows + fold the narration row — apply ladder

Per `docs/plans/protection-matrix-catalogue-track-and-rows.md`.
Sequenced after the self-recovery seal (main `ca0241b1`) so both new
guard symbols exist and resolve. Single-component amendment on the
EXISTING `framework/protection-matrix/` component (first seal was
`68fb6f8`); this seal advances the existing sidecar.

Three protection-matrix defects/owed-items closed in one cycle:

  - AC.PMTRACK.1 (outcome-altitude) — the source-of-truth catalogue
    `framework/protection-matrix/data/failure-mode-guard-matrix.yaml`
    was gitignored by the over-broad `.gitignore` `data/` rule, so it
    shipped UNTRACKED — a fresh clone resolved `default_catalogue_path()`
    to a missing file and could NOT load the flagship matrix. Fix: a
    `.gitignore` negation re-includes just this one hand-authored
    catalogue (the generated runtime `data/` dirs stay ignored) and the
    file is force-added. The AC asserts from `git ls-files` (NOT the
    working-tree copy) that the catalogue is tracked AND
    `load_catalogue(default_catalogue_path())` parses the full row set —
    it fails if the file is untracked/gitignored.

  - AC.PMROW.1 — the FM.PROCESS-DRIFT row (owed from the defined-workflow
    build) exists, schema-conformant, with a `guard_ref` resolving to the
    merged re-injection guard
    (`framework/tools/loam/src/loam_cli/flows/reinject.py:build_reinjection_context`).

  - AC.PMROW.2 — the FM.COMMS-PATH-DEAD row (self-recovery F-4) exists,
    schema-conformant, with a `guard_ref` resolving to the merged
    watchdog comms-liveness guard
    (`framework/self-correction/src/loam/self_correction/watchdog.py:ChannelVerdict`);
    AND the FM.NARRATION-NOT-ACTION row, formerly an empty-ref
    persona-discipline gap, is folded to bind the distress-detector
    (`framework/self-correction/hooks/distress_detector.py:classify_distress`)
    — its unfulfilled-claim class catches the narration-not-action
    distress shape on the inbound path.

  - AC.PMGEN.1 — the generated companion `docs/design/protection-matrix.md`
    is regenerated from the updated catalogue (the md↔yaml sync test
    stays green; the companion is GENERATED, never hand-edited).

Both new rows resolve to REAL importable symbols via the production
resolver — no hallucinated guard (the recursive-FM.HALLUCINATION risk the
matrix exists to prevent). Both ship `default_on: NO-PROGRAMMATIC`,
`class: floor` — VISIBLE gap rows (the guards exist + are sealed but
wiring into a live settings.json is owner-gated), not silent omissions.

The rows REFERENCE the other components' existing public symbols; they do
NOT edit those components. The fence stays `framework/protection-matrix/`
plus the two admitted universal paths (`.gitignore` negation + the
generated companion).

Surfaced (NOT fixed here — separate candidate): (1) the seal-fence
verifies committed diff scope but NOT that every runtime-required file is
git-tracked — a gitignored source file passes seal silently (this cycle's
AC.PMTRACK.1 catches it for THIS file; the general fix is a seal-time
"every runtime-resolved path is tracked" check). (2) the guard_ref
resolver (`derive.py:_symbol_defined_in`) matches `def`/`class` but NOT
`async def`, so an async guard symbol cannot be bound — `ChannelVerdict`
(a class) was selected for FM.COMMS-PATH-DEAD rather than the
`async def check_channel_and_self_heal` it wraps.

